      "chunk_type": "text",
      "text": "Protecting the speaker wire\nThe bare ends of the speaker cord can be affected by exposure to the elements. This is especially true of saltwater exposure. You may use a silicone caulking material, such as RTV adhesive, to protect the connections. It is commonly available at hardware stores. If you do use caulking, apply it only after the wires are connected and the knobs tightened down. Check the connections annually, and reapply as needed.",
      "content_region_ids": [
